**How to implement.** A fit's own account of its uncertainty moves into Optimization, for the Planner's layer 2 (001 §Q AT-2 '`predictedRelativeErrors`, `combinationVariance` (the Planner's layer 2 reuses them, §M)'; the S10.1 brief 'fitReportOf … predictedRelativeErrors, combinationVariance, differenceWeights'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) `fitReportOf` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:fitReportOf`), a function of one of our types, becomes the member `member this.report : FitQuality.FitReport` of `MuellerFitData` in `MuellerFitting.fs` (ELEV013), with its body: `FitQuality.reportFrom` over the residual and the solution as a `DesignVector`, with the final residuals. (2) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs`, `module FitUncertainty` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `RecoveryEnsembles.fs` (one `<Compile>` line, no comment). Its module doc, one to three lines: what a fit's covariance and Jacobian say about the uncertainty of its parameters and of their combinations, moved by spec 0050 S10.1 for the Planner (001 §M). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (3) In it: `type ParameterWeights = | ParameterWeights of float[]` with `value`, marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier("a weight vector over a fit's parameters in its scaling's axis order (R3): read whole against the covariance and the residual Jacobian")>]` (the S10.1 brief: float[] weight vectors are carriers). `type PredictedVariance = | PredictedVariance of double` with `value`, doc one line: the variance a fit's covariance predicts for a linear combination of its parameters, in scaled units. `predictedRelativeErrors` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:predictedRelativeErrors`) moves with its signature over `MuellerFitData` and body. `combinationVariance (quality : FitQuality.FitReport) (weights : ParameterWeights) : PredictedVariance` is today's `wᵀCw` double sum (`InverseFitHarness.fs:combinationVariance`) on the carrier's array. `differenceWeights (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) (plus : ParameterName) (minus : ParameterName) : Result<ParameterWeights, MuellerFitError>` answers, built without mutation, the vector holding 1.0 at `plus`'s axis, −1.0 at `minus`'s (−1.0 when they coincide, as today) and 0.0 elsewhere; an axis name that is not in `scaling.axes` is `Error (UnknownAxisErr <name>)`. (4) `MuellerFitError` gains `UnknownAxisErr of ParameterName` (no fitted parameter of that name). (5) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes the four. Callers: `fitReportOf first.fit` becomes `first.fit.report` in `MuellerInverseTests` and `BiaxialInverseTests`; in `MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact `pairVariance` is `combinationVariance quality (differenceWeights first.fit.scaling (ParameterName "n_e") (ParameterName "n_o") |> expectOk)`, read as `pairVariance.value` in `pairPrediction` and in the message. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the report, the conversion out of the scaled space and the quadratic form are unchanged. No test is added or removed. `MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact drives all four; `BiaxialInverseTests` (997 s) is not selected.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `MuellerFitData.report` MUST replace `fitReportOf`, `FitUncertainty.fs` MUST declare `ParameterWeights` (a `[<NumericCarrier>]`), `PredictedVariance`, `predictedRelativeErrors`, `combinationVariance` and `differenceWeights` (an unknown axis being `UnknownAxisErr`), compiled directly after `RecoveryEnsembles.fs`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.
